# Deliberate binary break in 1.9.0, relative to 1.8.0. See the release note in README.md.
#
# `object Traverse` is renamed to `object Visits`. The division it belongs to is sound — the
# engine takes a Visitor and returns a Visitor, while this facade builds a SimpleVisitor for the
# caller and returns a List[V] — but the three names in that area, Traversal, Traverse and
# Traversed, were distinguishable only by inflection, and the inflection did not map to the
# roles. `Visits` says what the caller gets back: the visits, in order.
#
# Traverse was introduced in 1.8.0 and so carries one release of history, which made it the
# cheapest of the three to rename. The engine keeps the name Traversal.
#
# Under PVP, 1.8.0 -> 1.9.0 is a major bump, so this break is permitted. See
# https://github.com/rchillyard/Visitor/issues/48 for the release it travels with.
#
# NOTE: contrary to what the comment in build.sbt long claimed, this file does NOT retire itself
# when previousRelease moves past 1.8.0. sbt-mima applies every *.backwards.excludes file in
# this directory, whatever it is named, so these two lines stay in force until the file is
# deleted by hand. Delete it once 1.9.0 is published and previousRelease has moved on, after
# checking that mimaReportBinaryIssues is still clean without it. See
# https://github.com/rchillyard/Visitor/issues/50
#
# The exact filter lines below are MiMa's own suggestions from the failing run, not hand-written.

ProblemFilters.exclude[MissingClassProblem]("com.phasmidsoftware.visitor.core.Traverse")
ProblemFilters.exclude[MissingClassProblem]("com.phasmidsoftware.visitor.core.Traverse$")

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Behaviours.scala is split into one file per typeclass family (1.9.0).
#
# It had become a grab-bag of five unrelated typeclasses whose only common feature was that
# nobody had found a home for them: Evaluable, Neighbours, VisitedSet, Frontier and CostUpdate.
# Each now has its own file, named for the typeclass it holds.
#
# No logic changed, and nothing moved out of the package, so this is source-compatible: callers'
# imports and implicit resolution are unaffected. It is nevertheless a binary break, because in
# Scala 3 the top-level definitions of a file compile into a synthetic class named after that
# file. Moving a top-level given from Behaviours.scala to Frontier.scala renames its enclosing
# class, and Behaviours$package ceases to exist. The traits themselves are ordinary classes and
# move for free; the seven entries below are the synthetic holder and the top-level givens.
#
# This is why the split was done in 1.9.0, which is a major bump under PVP and was already
# breaking for the Traverse rename, rather than left for later.
#
# The exact filter lines below are MiMa's own suggestions from the failing run, not hand-written.

ProblemFilters.exclude[MissingClassProblem]("com.phasmidsoftware.visitor.core.Behaviours$package")
ProblemFilters.exclude[MissingClassProblem]("com.phasmidsoftware.visitor.core.Behaviours$package$")
ProblemFilters.exclude[MissingClassProblem]("com.phasmidsoftware.visitor.core.Behaviours$package$given_CostUpdate_W_F")
ProblemFilters.exclude[MissingClassProblem]("com.phasmidsoftware.visitor.core.Behaviours$package$given_Frontier_IndexedPrioQueue$")
ProblemFilters.exclude[MissingClassProblem]("com.phasmidsoftware.visitor.core.Behaviours$package$given_Frontier_PrioQueue$")
ProblemFilters.exclude[MissingClassProblem]("com.phasmidsoftware.visitor.core.Behaviours$package$given_Frontier_Queue$")
ProblemFilters.exclude[MissingClassProblem]("com.phasmidsoftware.visitor.core.Behaviours$package$given_Frontier_Stack$")

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The misc package is eliminated (1.9.0). See
# https://github.com/rchillyard/Visitor/issues/31
#
# misc carried a partial, parallel copy of core's journal hierarchy. Its IterableJournal,
# ListJournal and QueueJournal duplicated core's by name and behaviour, which is a trap rather
# than a convenience: two same-named types in one library, differing only in a field name. Those
# three are DELETED; core's equivalents stand.
#
# Everything else MOVED into core unchanged: AppendableWriter, NonAppendable,
# FunctionMappedJournal, AbstractMapJournal, MapJournal and FunctionMapJournal. A move is still
# a binary break, the package being part of the name, which is why they appear below despite
# still existing.
#
# For a caller the source fix is an import: com.phasmidsoftware.visitor.misc.X becomes
# com.phasmidsoftware.visitor.core.X, for the deleted duplicates as well as the moved types,
# since core has same-named equivalents. The one place that is not mechanical is field access on
# the two duplicated journals, where core uses shorter names: ListJournal.list is now
# ListJournal.xs, and QueueJournal.queue is now QueueJournal.q. The README records this.
#
# The exact filter lines below are MiMa's own suggestions from the failing run, not hand-written.

ProblemFilters.exclude[MissingClassProblem]("com.phasmidsoftware.visitor.misc.AbstractMapJournal")
ProblemFilters.exclude[MissingClassProblem]("com.phasmidsoftware.visitor.misc.AppendableWriter")
ProblemFilters.exclude[MissingClassProblem]("com.phasmidsoftware.visitor.misc.AppendableWriter$")
ProblemFilters.exclude[MissingClassProblem]("com.phasmidsoftware.visitor.misc.FunctionMapJournal")
ProblemFilters.exclude[MissingClassProblem]("com.phasmidsoftware.visitor.misc.FunctionMapJournal$")
ProblemFilters.exclude[MissingClassProblem]("com.phasmidsoftware.visitor.misc.FunctionMappedJournal")
ProblemFilters.exclude[MissingClassProblem]("com.phasmidsoftware.visitor.misc.IterableJournal")
ProblemFilters.exclude[MissingClassProblem]("com.phasmidsoftware.visitor.misc.ListJournal")
ProblemFilters.exclude[MissingClassProblem]("com.phasmidsoftware.visitor.misc.ListJournal$")
ProblemFilters.exclude[MissingClassProblem]("com.phasmidsoftware.visitor.misc.MapJournal")
ProblemFilters.exclude[MissingClassProblem]("com.phasmidsoftware.visitor.misc.MapJournal$")
ProblemFilters.exclude[MissingClassProblem]("com.phasmidsoftware.visitor.misc.NonAppendable")
ProblemFilters.exclude[MissingClassProblem]("com.phasmidsoftware.visitor.misc.NonAppendable$")
ProblemFilters.exclude[MissingClassProblem]("com.phasmidsoftware.visitor.misc.QueueJournal")
ProblemFilters.exclude[MissingClassProblem]("com.phasmidsoftware.visitor.misc.QueueJournal$")
